@startsalt
' Screen: Org Settings — Freeball Section
' User Stories:
'   - As an org admin, I want to configure the default runner model for freeball generation
'   - As an org admin, I want to set default depth and total limits for freeball traversal
'   - As an org admin, I want to configure confidence thresholds for routing decisions
'   - As an org admin, I want to toggle learning mode to control auto-promotion behavior

{
  ' Top nav
  {
    <b>codefre.sh</b> | Scripts | Runs | Review Queue | <b>Settings</b>
    .
    <i>Acme Engineering</i> | keith@noizu.com
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Organization Settings — Acme Engineering</b>
  }
  --
  {
    ' Sidebar
    {+
      <b>Settings</b>
      --
      General
      Members
      API Tokens
      SSO
      <b>Freeball</b>
      Webhooks
      Audit Log
    }
    |
    ' Content
    {
      <b>Freeball Configuration</b>
      <i>These defaults apply org-wide. Scripts may override at the script level.</i>
      ==
      {+
        <b>Runner Model</b>
        --
        ^gpt-4o                                        ^
        <i>Model used to generate and evaluate freeball prompts.\nOptions: gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, claude-3-5-sonnet, claude-3-haiku</i>
        --
        <b>System Prompt Reference</b>
        ^freeball-default-v2 (built-in)                ^
        <i>System prompt injected into the runner for freeball generation.\nCustom prompts can be managed in the Prompts library.</i>
      }
      ==
      {+
        <b>Traversal Limits</b>
        --
        <b>freeball_max_depth</b>   <i>(max hops from trigger node)</i>
        [3     ]
        <i>Recommended: 3. Higher values increase coverage but raise cost and latency.</i>
        --
        <b>freeball_max_total</b>   <i>(max freeballs per run)</i>
        [25    ]
        <i>Recommended: 25. Cap total freeballs generated per run to control spend.</i>
      }
      ==
      {+
        <b>Confidence Thresholds</b>
        <i>Used to route freeballs to different actions automatically.</i>
        --
        <b>Low threshold</b>   <i>— below this, flag for mandatory human review</i>
        [0.50  ]
        --
        <b>Medium threshold</b>   <i>— between low and high, suggest review</i>
        [0.70  ]
        --
        <b>High threshold</b>   <i>— above this, eligible for auto-approve (if learning mode enabled)</i>
        [0.85  ]
        --
        <i>Current routing: &lt;0.50 = mandatory review | 0.50-0.85 = suggested review | &gt;0.85 = auto-approve (if enabled)</i>
      }
      ==
      {+
        <b>Learning Mode</b>
        --
        [X] <b>Enable learning mode</b>
        <i>When enabled, freeballs with confidence above the high threshold are automatically\napproved and promoted as expectations without requiring human review.\n\nDisable in regulated environments or when human sign-off is required for all changes.</i>
        --
        <color:orange>Learning mode is active. 14 freeballs were auto-promoted in the last 7 days.</color>
        [View Auto-Promoted Log]
      }
      ==
      {
        [Save Freeball Settings] | [Reset to Defaults]
      }
    }
  }
}

@endsalt
